+
+A review is split into **lenses**: each lens is one reviewer with one checklist, so no checklist gets lost in a long one. Pick the lenses that apply, then start their reviewers **in parallel** (one message, several Agent calls).
+
+| Lens | Runs for | Runs when | Reviewer | Checks |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `code` | each bead and branch review | always | `implementer-sonnet` | the checklist under "Code lens" below |
+| `security` | each bead | the diff touches auth, permissions, remote host access, the audit log, subprocess execution, path handling, secrets or tokens | `implementer-sonnet` | authorization on every new entry point; input validation and injection (SQL, command, path traversal, prompt); secrets in code, logs or tests; token and crypto handling; malicious-case tests exist for the security-relevant code (see next-task-write-tests) |
+| `ui` | each bead | changed files under `frontend/` | `implementer-sonnet` | follows the apple-design skill (read .claude/skills/apple-design/SKILL.md): design tokens instead of literal values, spacing and typography, loading, empty, error and disabled states, both themes, accessibility (roles, labels, focus order, contrast) |
+| `ux` | branch review | changed files under `frontend/` | `implementer-sonnet` | the user flows the work set adds work end to end across its beads: each new screen or action is reachable, navigation and wording are consistent, error and empty paths lead somewhere, no dead ends, and the e2e specs cover the main journey |
